00:47:51.990 --> 00:47:52.290
No!

00:48:07.420 --> 00:48:07.780
Did you call her?

00:48:09.770 --> 00:48:11.410
What's wrong, miss?

00:48:11.790 --> 00:48:17.050
I put it on.

00:48:18.760 --> 00:48:19.580
We'll fix it.

00:48:19.920 --> 00:48:24.270
What do you mean?

00:48:24.570 --> 00:48:25.650
It's a short circuit.

00:48:26.690 --> 00:48:28.970
He's leaving. He's going to Rio.

00:48:29.290 --> 00:48:29.690
Already?

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:35.080
When is he leaving?

00:48:35.320 --> 00:48:35.720
Today.

00:48:37.780 --> 00:48:39.240
And you can't remember him?

00:48:39.380 --> 00:48:41.420
And you can't think of him?

00:48:41.660 --> 00:48:44.180
Then kill him.

00:48:47.140 --> 00:48:48.260
Suicide doesn't mean anything to you.

00:48:50.070 --> 00:48:53.210
Do you have an affair?

00:48:53.610 --> 00:48:53.930
No.

00:48:54.640 --> 00:48:55.960
Then go with him.

00:48:56.760 --> 00:48:57.820
What can it do?

00:48:58.100 --> 00:48:59.080
Did he rent a cabin or the whole boat?

00:48:59.500 --> 00:48:59.860
Cabin.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.260
Cabin? There's still room for you on board.

00:49:02.440 --> 00:49:03.700
If you like him, don't let him go.

00:49:03.820 --> 00:49:06.560
Love is like electricity. For it to work, you have to contract it.

00:49:06.950 --> 00:49:07.490
I'm telling you.

00:49:07.690 --> 00:49:17.730
You save my life! You're so sweet!

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:34.860
It's a story, a counter-bomb, an anthropophage!

00:49:35.660 --> 00:49:36.520
Shame on you!

00:49:36.620 --> 00:49:37.480
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:37.700 --> 00:49:38.600
I had her.

00:49:38.660 --> 00:49:39.300
Tell me the truth!

00:49:39.620 --> 00:49:40.690
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:41.610 --> 00:49:42.130
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:42.500 --> 00:49:44.240
Don't scold her, she's a child.

00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:44.620
You?

00:49:45.230 --> 00:49:46.850
Tell me the truth!

00:49:47.300 --> 00:49:47.620
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:47.920 --> 00:49:50.890
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:52.940 --> 00:49:57.660
The train leaves in half an hour.

00:49:57.840 --> 00:49:58.760
Where is Miss Barbara?

00:49:58.900 --> 00:49:59.560
I'll be right back.

00:50:00.280 --> 00:50:02.430
I'm in my bath. I'm completely naked.

00:50:03.610 --> 00:50:03.970
Speak again.

00:50:04.290 --> 00:50:07.530
Oh, dear little Trump, here I am. I'm getting out of my bath.

00:50:07.970 --> 00:50:10.000
A bath? She's taking a bath.

00:50:10.400 --> 00:50:12.180
For the soap, count on me.

00:50:12.380 --> 00:50:14.230
In 23 minutes.

00:50:23.200 --> 00:50:27.240
Love is stronger than death. How long will it last?

00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:29.880
In 20 minutes. There's no time limit.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.520
I remember when I was a sailor, you thought I was out of my mind.

00:50:32.660 --> 00:50:34.120
I'll tell you another day. We don't have time today.

00:50:35.020 --> 00:50:36.760
Don't be afraid. You can grab my neck.

00:50:36.940 --> 00:50:38.740
You're good against me. There's no danger.

00:50:38.940 --> 00:50:39.980
How tall are you?

00:50:40.640 --> 00:50:41.000
Sixty.

00:50:41.320 --> 00:50:42.500
Sixty? You're in good health.

00:50:42.640 --> 00:50:43.100
Come on, let's go.

00:50:45.750 --> 00:50:48.320
Hold on.

00:50:48.730 --> 00:50:48.970
Hold on.

00:51:00.828 --> 00:51:04.828
Nyan-Tik-Tik-Nan Nyan-Tik-Tik-Nan

00:51:05.116 --> 00:51:07.116
Thank you for your viewing.

00:51:07.196 --> 00:51:09.196
Thank you for your viewing.

00:51:10.204 --> 00:51:12.204
Thank you for watching.

00:51:13.404 --> 00:51:15.404
Thank you for watching.

00:51:35.600 --> 00:51:43.760
Well, yes! He cheated on me, he cheated on this woman!

00:51:43.900 --> 00:51:44.480
What woman?

00:51:45.900 --> 00:51:47.870
His bracelet!

00:51:48.370 --> 00:51:48.750
I don't have it!

00:51:50.830 --> 00:51:51.330
It's not true!

00:51:51.470 --> 00:51:53.800
It's true, it's clear!

00:52:10.040 --> 00:52:10.480
I got to take the subway.

00:52:10.800 --> 00:52:11.960
I got to take the subway.

00:52:12.140 --> 00:52:12.840
I'll finish tomorrow.

00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:13.960
Yes, yes, yes.

00:52:14.080 --> 00:52:24.840
See you, Claire.

00:52:25.200 --> 00:52:25.680
Bye, my friend!

00:52:27.050 --> 00:52:27.670
Bye, my friend!

00:52:28.250 --> 00:52:28.330
Bye.

00:52:38.320 --> 00:52:38.620
Read it.

00:52:38.660 --> 00:52:55.610
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:53:14.300 --> 00:53:17.920
What are you doing, my little dog?

00:53:49.680 --> 00:53:51.200
I don't know. He must have fallen off a bridge.

00:53:51.480 --> 00:53:57.060
We found him on the bridge. Let's go get a doctor.

00:54:02.910 --> 00:54:07.110
I'm sorry. You're hurting me.

00:54:07.230 --> 00:54:11.470
My little Zouzou!

00:54:15.040 --> 00:54:17.210
You killed me!

00:54:17.910 --> 00:54:28.080
Ladies and gentlemen, tonight, for the first time in your life...

00:54:32.810 --> 00:54:33.250
What are you doing?

00:55:21.630 --> 00:55:22.430
Clare has never had any friends.

00:55:22.630 --> 00:55:24.590
We don't dance?

00:55:25.050 --> 00:55:26.000
No, we don't.

00:55:27.350 --> 00:55:29.870
It's funny, there are days like that when we're not on the train.

00:55:30.480 --> 00:55:30.860
I don't know why.

00:55:33.200 --> 00:55:36.110
Cigarettes? I'll get some. There's tobacco.

00:55:37.010 --> 00:55:37.810
Take care of yourself.

00:55:54.320 --> 00:55:55.800
You're not going to get away like that.

00:55:55.920 --> 00:55:56.580
Give me the pen.

00:55:56.940 --> 00:55:57.960
You're in the way of the jewellery.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:01.070
I don't owe you anything.

00:56:01.570 --> 00:56:03.190
Give me my bag or I'll kill you.

00:56:03.350 --> 00:56:04.030
I don't owe you anything.

00:56:04.580 --> 00:56:05.760
I don't owe you anything.

00:56:05.940 --> 00:56:06.980
I want my share.

00:56:47.400 --> 00:56:49.190
I saw him at my place the other night.

00:56:49.410 --> 00:56:52.650
You know, it reminds me...

00:56:52.650 --> 00:56:53.610
But it wasn't him!

00:56:54.130 --> 00:56:55.830
He was looking for cigarettes!

00:56:56.670 --> 00:56:58.450
Tell them you were looking for cigarettes!

00:56:58.910 --> 00:56:59.660
Tell them!

00:57:04.350 --> 00:57:05.600
I don't know, let's see then.

00:57:05.780 --> 00:57:06.580
I don't know.

00:57:06.800 --> 00:57:16.280
You say it's not me, you're kidding.

00:57:16.600 --> 00:57:17.140
It's Pio!

00:57:45.324 --> 00:57:46.324
Thank you very much.

00:58:17.560 --> 00:58:17.900
He's innocent.

00:58:18.280 --> 00:58:19.460
You have to prove it.

00:58:20.680 --> 00:58:21.500
He's not even born yet.

00:58:21.620 --> 00:58:25.020
I'm asking you what this idiot needed to buy cigarettes.

00:58:25.300 --> 00:58:26.020
I asked him.

00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:28.320
First of all, I had defended you from smoking.

00:58:30.190 --> 00:58:31.130
If I had defended him or not.

00:58:31.990 --> 00:58:33.570
A mother can do anything.

00:58:34.510 --> 00:58:36.650
Do you see how bad it can be?

00:58:39.140 --> 00:58:43.110
He went to pick them up, but he didn't know what he was doing.

00:58:43.830 --> 00:58:46.490
Mum, we must do something for him.

00:58:46.610 --> 00:58:49.230
We must. To go to prison, we must steal some money.

00:58:49.370 --> 00:58:51.050
But to get out of it, we must give it. And a lot.

00:58:51.330 --> 00:58:52.980
There are innocent people who are poor.

00:58:53.740 --> 00:58:55.500
A poor innocent man is a crook.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:00.540
You don't have any news?

00:59:00.780 --> 00:59:02.000
No, no one knows what happened.

00:59:02.320 --> 00:59:04.940
Did you go to the police station?

00:59:05.490 --> 00:59:08.200
Yes. The police officer wasn't there.

00:59:08.910 --> 00:59:09.770
He's never been there.

00:59:10.250 --> 00:59:13.990
Poor people. What are they going to do?

00:59:14.690 --> 00:59:18.510
I'll go see his lawyer.

00:59:18.790 --> 00:59:19.940
Who is it?

00:59:20.260 --> 00:59:21.540
A guy named L'Office.

00:59:21.880 --> 00:59:23.440
Don't let him tell my little story.

00:59:23.760 --> 00:59:24.880
Of course not.

00:59:25.610 --> 00:59:28.180
Zouzou, if we had some fries, it wouldn't be like this.

00:59:28.300 --> 00:59:29.620
For the money.

00:59:30.030 --> 00:59:30.290
I've got money.

00:59:30.690 --> 00:59:33.260
You want to call your villager?

00:59:34.030 --> 00:59:40.440
I'm so jealous.

00:59:40.820 --> 00:59:41.750
Give me the mustard.

00:59:42.050 --> 00:59:44.300
I've taken some field lessons and I'm doing business now.

00:59:44.640 --> 00:59:45.660
You're getting me in debt.

00:59:45.880 --> 00:59:46.620
What do you have to earn?

00:59:46.980 --> 00:59:49.250
With the morning classes, it's 2,000 a month.

00:59:49.370 --> 00:59:50.820
It's nice with the running time.

00:59:51.380 --> 00:59:55.410
Soon, we'll have a villa in Vincent with a manager and a accountant.

00:59:56.450 --> 00:59:57.010
It's our job.

00:59:57.350 --> 00:59:59.410
If we have talent, we can do everything.

01:00:00.160 --> 01:00:02.510
I bet you'll see what he's talking about.

01:00:02.660 --> 01:00:04.220
I even have a cheque book.

01:00:05.030 --> 01:00:05.890
Here you go.

01:00:06.400 --> 01:00:08.500
He's gone. It's the English week.

01:00:08.680 --> 01:00:11.610
I'll pick you up tomorrow.

01:00:12.180 --> 01:00:14.320
I want to see Mr. Trump.

01:00:14.540 --> 01:00:15.820
Do you think he'll pick me up?

01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:17.440
How can he pick you up?

01:00:19.810 --> 01:00:26.210
It's over. When we wanted you, you left.

01:00:27.620 --> 01:00:29.060
Now that we don't think of you anymore, here you are.

01:00:30.060 --> 01:00:30.560
What do you want?

01:00:30.860 --> 01:00:38.310
I need a lot, a lot of money.

01:00:38.840 --> 01:00:41.420
You're all the same. You think I'm a chrysosome.

01:00:41.760 --> 01:00:43.430
What do you think you're doing?

01:00:44.420 --> 01:00:45.240
Thank you.

01:00:45.520 --> 01:00:46.280
I'll give you a little money.

01:00:47.640 --> 01:00:48.530
You want a job?

01:00:49.090 --> 01:00:49.850
I'll give you success.

01:00:50.210 --> 01:00:51.250
Be a teacher in front of the public.

01:00:51.570 --> 01:00:53.670
I'll give you a gold medal.

01:00:53.830 --> 01:00:55.950
Or an experience like this, Miss Barbara.

01:00:56.570 --> 01:00:57.510
No, no.

01:00:57.670 --> 01:00:59.170
It's enough for a man's life.

01:00:59.250 --> 01:00:59.970
Oh, my God!

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.520
Jassierie? No, no, not that one.

01:01:03.240 --> 01:01:06.320
Oh, it's someone, gentlemen.

01:01:07.200 --> 01:01:10.620
I swear it wasn't a small matter to get the permission,

01:01:10.800 --> 01:01:14.940
and at what cost, to present it exclusively to the Parisian public.

01:01:15.080 --> 01:01:17.130
All the cities in South America were fighting for it.

01:01:17.210 --> 01:01:19.130
Its tour at the Transvaal was triumphant.

01:01:19.330 --> 01:01:20.850
London was a gold mine.

01:01:21.050 --> 01:01:23.630
Its train passed everywhere. It ran for miles and miles.

01:01:24.130 --> 01:01:26.990
The Camelia's voice was hoarse, its favorite flower.

01:01:27.150 --> 01:01:29.640
But it was the same thing that attracted it. Paris!

01:01:30.320 --> 01:01:33.100
I saw the light. And here's why, Zouzou.

01:01:33.200 --> 01:01:34.620
Are you going to play a role?

01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:37.040
No, it's my job, as I say to the journalists.

01:01:37.540 --> 01:01:39.260
As long as we tell them good stories, they'll enjoy it.

01:01:40.080 --> 01:01:41.640
But, for God's sake! The horizon!

01:01:42.000 --> 01:01:44.280
Oh, fetishes!

01:01:44.480 --> 01:01:46.780
What are you doing?

01:01:46.940 --> 01:01:47.460
The moments in my heart!

01:01:47.540 --> 01:01:47.900
Which ones?

01:01:48.040 --> 01:01:48.520
The one when you...

01:02:20.090 --> 01:02:26.120
Oh my God! Make me a success!

01:02:26.400 --> 01:02:27.220
Count on it!

01:02:31.440 --> 01:02:36.900
Don't get angry, you have time. It's the forest that's passing by.

01:02:36.900 --> 01:02:39.480
Come on, I'll take a break. I shouldn't have told you that.

01:02:39.600 --> 01:02:40.960
Take a break.

01:02:41.040 --> 01:02:41.400
No.

01:02:41.670 --> 01:02:44.120
Oh, you've changed your mind.

01:02:44.380 --> 01:02:46.820
Oh, because you're still thinking about him.

01:02:47.120 --> 01:02:49.980
Are we printing?

01:02:50.440 --> 01:02:51.250
No, impossible!

01:02:51.870 --> 01:02:52.700
We are...

01:02:54.390 --> 01:02:55.430
They are more beautiful.

01:03:01.630 --> 01:03:03.850
We're not going to keep him in jail until the end of his life!

01:03:04.110 --> 01:03:06.360
You're spending so much money on him!

01:03:06.560 --> 01:03:08.210
What did the lawyer say to you?

01:03:30.030 --> 01:03:30.310
Thank you.

01:07:00.060 --> 01:07:00.300
Thank you.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:33.650
The most beautiful car of your dreams

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:01.740
Far far away under our skies

01:09:01.740 --> 01:09:04.000
I lived happy days

01:09:04.750 --> 01:09:07.770
And it's all over

01:09:07.770 --> 01:09:09.670
Alone in my exile today

01:09:10.190 --> 01:09:12.690
I sing the prairie

01:10:00.060 --> 01:10:01.880
More freedom.

01:10:55.470 --> 01:10:59.240
Where are you going?

01:11:00.160 --> 01:11:01.440
I had a lot, a lot of success.

01:11:02.630 --> 01:11:03.210
I'm not surprised.

01:11:03.750 --> 01:11:08.910
Well, they saved him!

01:11:09.230 --> 01:11:10.190
That's it, he's going crazy!

01:11:10.310 --> 01:11:10.850
Look, look!

01:11:11.250 --> 01:11:14.980
There! The man who killed Julon!

01:11:15.060 --> 01:11:15.600
It's him!

01:11:18.280 --> 01:11:18.640
Horrible!

01:11:23.090 --> 01:11:23.450
Do it!

01:11:23.470 --> 01:11:24.650
But I'm leaving!

01:11:24.850 --> 01:11:25.750
Oh, you're leaving!

01:11:26.250 --> 01:11:27.030
Quick, quick, my chin!

01:11:27.330 --> 01:11:27.850
But you're crazy!

01:11:28.380 --> 01:11:28.980
Well, he saw it!

01:11:31.050 --> 01:11:33.510
You'll go one day, another day, tomorrow, the day after tomorrow, when you'll have time!

01:11:33.730 --> 01:11:34.070
But...

01:11:34.070 --> 01:11:35.210
The assassination is starting!

01:11:35.590 --> 01:11:36.450
But I'm sure...

01:11:37.180 --> 01:11:38.960
I can't give you your shoes, it's impossible!

01:11:39.700 --> 01:11:41.120
But think about it, Zouzou!

01:11:41.240 --> 01:11:42.420
All of Paris is in the hall!

01:11:42.640 --> 01:11:44.060
There are ministers, ambassadors!

01:11:44.840 --> 01:11:45.140
I'm lying!

01:11:45.650 --> 01:11:46.330
Oh, you won't go!

01:11:46.730 --> 01:11:47.490
You won't go!

01:11:47.750 --> 01:11:49.330
Or you'll put one on my body!

01:11:51.810 --> 01:11:52.430
What are we going to do?

01:11:52.650 --> 01:11:54.750
The assassination is starting!

01:12:00.188 --> 01:12:00.688
Austin!

01:13:00.190 --> 01:13:05.080
What's that?

01:13:05.400 --> 01:13:07.450
He's gone! He's like a fool!

01:13:07.690 --> 01:13:08.650
What about his boss?

01:13:08.870 --> 01:13:12.050
Tell him! He's going to die when he learns that!

01:13:12.310 --> 01:13:13.010
Where did she go?

01:13:13.190 --> 01:13:14.050
What did I tell you?

01:13:15.110 --> 01:13:16.690
She saw a picture in the newspaper.

01:13:16.690 --> 01:13:17.990
She said it was her killer.

01:13:18.350 --> 01:13:19.010
I don't understand.

01:13:19.980 --> 01:13:20.780
What a story!

01:13:22.390 --> 01:13:26.940
Are you sure it's him?

01:13:27.480 --> 01:13:29.080
Absolutely sure, Mr. Commissioner.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.520
Keep it well, miss. You can be wrong, it's very serious.

01:13:33.060 --> 01:13:34.840
No, I'm not wrong.

01:13:35.020 --> 01:13:36.660
Are you sure?

01:13:37.990 --> 01:13:39.690
He came out in front of me in the street.

01:13:39.770 --> 01:13:42.460
I saw his hand on the street.

01:13:44.420 --> 01:13:46.010
It wasn't me! I told you it wasn't me!

01:13:46.250 --> 01:13:47.750
What's so extraordinary about his hand?

01:13:48.080 --> 01:13:48.960
It's as big as his finger.

01:13:49.180 --> 01:13:53.310
He also has a scar.

01:13:54.120 --> 01:13:54.780
I told you it wasn't me!

01:13:56.930 --> 01:13:58.530
Show me your hand if it's not you!

01:13:58.750 --> 01:13:59.550
I told you it wasn't me!

01:14:00.220 --> 01:14:03.010
Come on, bring him in.

01:14:03.010 --> 01:14:07.600
Sit down, mademoiselle.

01:14:10.050 --> 01:14:12.720
Now tell me how it all happened.

01:14:13.040 --> 01:14:16.720
It was the day of Papa Mele's death.

01:14:16.720 --> 01:14:18.080
It was raining.

01:14:19.160 --> 01:14:20.620
Jean and Claire were dancing.

01:14:21.300 --> 01:14:27.080
Come on!

01:15:30.560 --> 01:15:32.900
Go on! I said go on!

01:15:33.160 --> 01:15:35.070
Go on! Go on!

01:16:00.250 --> 01:16:00.910
I've never seen that before.

01:16:00.950 --> 01:16:02.750
I saw it 30 days ago.

01:16:05.870 --> 01:16:10.230
My dear, my only friend, you alone can tell me about it.

01:16:10.610 --> 01:16:12.210
Yes, but I dance very badly.

01:16:12.550 --> 01:16:13.470
Barbara, where is Barbara?

01:16:14.070 --> 01:16:15.510
She sent me a postcard.

01:16:15.770 --> 01:16:17.210
Let her come, we'll go get her.

01:16:17.570 --> 01:16:18.610
Do you need it right now?

01:16:18.650 --> 01:16:19.090
Immediately.

01:16:19.770 --> 01:16:21.640
But she's in Rio de Janeiro.

01:16:21.880 --> 01:16:22.680
In Rio de Janeiro.

01:16:23.100 --> 01:16:23.460
She's here.

01:16:23.740 --> 01:16:23.960
What?

01:16:24.060 --> 01:16:24.520
She's here.

01:16:24.660 --> 01:16:25.260
She's in her room.

01:16:25.500 --> 01:16:26.380
Go get her.

01:16:26.480 --> 01:16:26.680
She's coming.

01:16:28.380 --> 01:16:29.780
Death!

01:16:33.360 --> 01:16:35.510
Where have you been? It's a shame!

01:16:36.110 --> 01:16:37.410
Hurry up, Josette!

01:16:37.550 --> 01:16:38.250
Listen to her!

01:16:39.750 --> 01:16:40.850
Let her go!

